      "message": "There\u0027s a subtle difference - `SkPath::getLastPt` resets the out param to {0,0} on failure, but with the `std::optional` version we don\u0027t get that behavior (and `SkPoint` does not have a default initializer).  So we need to initialize it explicitly in case of failure.\n\n... or, `std::optional` has this cool `value_or` helper to handle this pattern:\n\n```\n   const SkPoint currentPoint \u003d this-\u003egetLastPt().value_or({0, 0});\n\n   return this-\u003earcTo(...);\n```",
